::Using Git::
How does the .gitignore file help in managing a Git repository?
{
~ It increases the repository size.
= It prevents accidental tracking of unnecessary files like logs and build artifacts.
~ It commits sensitive files like passwords.
~ It fetches untracked files automatically.
}

::Using Git::
What happens if a file that was previously tracked by Git is added to the .gitignore file?
{
~ Git will stop tracking the file immediately.
~ The file will be deleted from the repository.
~ Git will ignore both the file and its previous versions.
= The file will still be tracked, but new changes won't be.
}
